.TH DIFFVIM-COMPUTE 1 "2026-08-16" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim-compute \- external diff computer for diffvim (C, C++, Rust, Go variants)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim-compute-<lang>
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diffvim-compute-<lang>
.B \-\-diff
.RI <patchfile>
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diffvim-compute-<lang>
.B \-\-diff
.B \-
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diffvim-compute-<lang>
.B \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim-compute
is the external diff computer used by
.BR diffvim (1)
(via the --precomputed flag).
Four implementations exist, all producing byte-for-byte identical output:

.TP
.B diffvim-compute-c
C reference implementation. The others are validated against this one.
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-cpp
C++ port. Identical algorithm, modern C++ data structures.
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-rust
Rust port. Identical algorithm, Rust idioms.
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-go
Go port. Identical algorithm, Go idioms.

All four read two files (or a unified diff) and write a precomputed
diff file in the line-oriented format that
.B "diffvim --precomputed FILE"
consumes.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I oldfile
Old version of the file (two-file mode).
.TP
.I newfile
New version of the file (two-file mode).
.TP
.I outputfile
Where to write the precomputed diff.
.TP
.I patchfile
A unified diff file to read instead of two separate files (with
.BR \-\-diff ).
Use
.B \-
to read the diff from stdin.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm lcs|myers|patience
Diff algorithm (default:
.BR lcs ).
.TP
.B \-\-semantic-cleanup
Merge adjacent delete/insert pairs into keeps where possible.
.TP
.B \-\-word-diff
Batch word runs in char ops (instead of one char per op).
.TP
.B \-\-indent-aware
Treat indent-only changes specially (preserve indentation).
.TP
.B \-\-optimize-sequence
Reorder ops within a line so deletes come before inserts (default:
.IR on ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-optimize-sequence
Disable op reordering within a line.
.TP
.B \-\-left-to-right
Within each line, emit keeps (in original order), then deletes,
then inserts. Useful for left-to-right reading flow.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Read a unified diff instead of two files. Positional args become
(patchfile, outputfile).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_ALGORITHM
Same as
.B \-\-algorithm.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_SEMANTIC_CLEANUP
Set to
.I 1
to enable by default.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_WORD_DIFF
Set to
.I 1
to enable by default.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_INDENT_AWARE
Set to
.I 1
to enable by default.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_OPTIMIZE_SEQUENCE
Default
.IR 1 ;
set to
.I 0
to disable.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_LEFT_TO_RIGHT
Set to
.I 1
to enable by default.

.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
The output file is line-oriented:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# algorithm <name>
# semantic_cleanup <0|1>
# word_diff <0|1>
# indent_aware <0|1>
# optimize_sequence <0|1>
# left_to_right <0|1>
# hunk_count <N>
HUNK <line>
keep|delete|insert <code>
HUNK <line>
keep|delete|insert <code>
...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where
.I code
is the Unicode code point of the character (e.g. 97 for 'a', 10 for
newline). See
.I docs/PARSERS.md
for a full description of the format.

.SH TIMING OUTPUT
Timing information is printed to stderr:
.PP
.RS
.nf
compute: <ms> ms (total)
startup: <ms> ms (process start to first byte read)
.fi
.RE

.SH BUILD
.PP
.RS
.nf
make -C compute c       # build only the C variant
make -C compute cpp     # build only the C++ variant
make -C compute rust    # build only the Rust variant (requires rustc)
make -C compute go      # build only the Go variant (requires go)
make -C compute         # build all four
.fi
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-c old.py new.py /tmp/diff.txt
Compute the diff and write to
.IR /tmp/diff.txt .
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-c --algorithm patience --semantic-cleanup old.py new.py out.txt
Use Patience algorithm with semantic cleanup.
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-c --diff patch.diff out.txt
Read a unified diff and convert to diffvim format.
.TP
.B diffvim-compute-c --diff - out.txt < patch.diff
Read the diff from stdin.
.TP
.B compute/bin/diffvim-compute-c old.py new.py /tmp/diff.txt && diffvim --precomputed /tmp/diff.txt old.py new.py
Compute the diff with the C tool, then run diffvim with the precomputed file.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR diffvim-compare (1)
.br
.I docs/PARALLEL_COMPUTE.md
covers the architecture, parallelism opportunities, and benchmark
results.
.I docs/PARSERS.md
documents the output file format in detail.
.I docs/src/architecture.md
has the mdBook version.
